{
  // MinerData_Guard
  // Value: CONST_MIN_DATA_BOX_AMNT
  // The script a MinerData box actually carries. It binds the signer to the identity stamped in R5,
  // then runs the real rules out of a context variable after checking their hash.
  //
  // Keeping it small keeps the box small, which matters because this is the one box in the protocol
  // designed to sit untouched for years and Ergo prices collection by length.
  //
  // No op byte here: every MinerData path is the miner's own, so the signer script is unconditional
  // and the logic dispatches for itself.

  // REGISTERS
  // R4: commitments, owned by the logic
  // R5: the miner's hashed proposition bytes, 32 bytes. Read here because it is what the signer is
  // bound against, and the logic conserves it on every path.

  // CONSTANTS
  // CONST_MINERDATA_LOGIC_HASH: blake2b256 of the serialized value bytes of the MinerData logic

  // CONTEXT VARS
  // CTX_SIGNER(0): value bytes of the miner's signing proposition
  // CTX_OP(1): read by the logic, not here
  // CTX_LOGIC(64): serialized value bytes of the MinerData logic

  // ASSUMPTIONS - statements which can be assumed to be true due to other contracts enforcing them
  // during creation of this UTXO
  // MinerDictionary created this box: it pinned this script, the credential token, the initial
  // commitment, R5, and refused R6. Every later path preserves all of it.
  //
  // DELIBERATE OMISSIONS - conditions left out on purpose
  // Nothing here looks at the credential token, the value, the commitments or any output. All of that
  // belongs to the logic, or to the dictionary on the paths it drives, and duplicating it would cost
  // the bytes this contract exists to save.

  val CTX_LOGIC = getVar[Coll[Byte]](64).get

  val signerProp = executeFromVar[SigmaProp](0)

  val authenticLogic = blake2b256( CTX_LOGIC ) == CONST_MINERDATA_LOGIC_HASH
  // The identity this box speaks for. Binding it here is what stops one miner spending another's
  // data box.
  val authenticMiner = blake2b256( signerProp.propBytes ) == SELF.R5[Coll[Byte]].get

  sigmaProp(authenticLogic && authenticMiner) && signerProp && executeFromVar[SigmaProp](64)
}
